# Test Conventions

## Structure
- `tests/unit/` — pure unit tests, no network, no filesystem I/O
- `tests/integration/` — hits live SOS site; mark `@pytest.mark.integration`
- `tests/fixtures/early_voting/` — small HTML/CSV/JSON samples

## Mocking httpx
Use `respx` to mock httpx requests in unit tests:
```python
import respx
import httpx

@respx.mock
def test_election_parse():
    respx.get("https://earlyvoting.texas-election.com/...").mock(
        return_value=httpx.Response(200, text=FIXTURE_HTML)
    )
```

## Fixture rules
- Use the smallest county (Loving County, townId=151, 6 rows) for roster fixtures
- Redact or synthesize VOTER_NAME and ID_VOTER in committed fixtures
- Never commit real PII in test fixtures

## Assertion style
- Assert on model fields, not raw dicts
- Always assert ID fields remain strings: `assert isinstance(record.voter_id, str)`
